      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-10-04T09:41:06Z",
      "note": "Reviewed anchor, defect, direct artifact and complete age history. Etherscan V2 getsourcecode for executionAddress identifies verified MatezStakingProgram (Solidity 0.7.6, non-proxy). stake quotes uint128(amnt) then credits untruncated amnt; claim(3,...) checks those inflated balances. Source-3 receipt/trace shows 16 stake(340282366920938463463374607431768211456) calls, zero MATEZ transferFrom amounts, and a successful reward payout. Full paginated getLogs upgrade_package(uint256,uint256), blocks 40608448 through block 44926244, returns 4382 events: 3531 stakes of exactly 2^128 in 84 transactions, first source-3 at 44220865:1; all preceding stakes are below uint128 overflow. Source-4 top-level creation receipt establishes block 40608448:27 and creator. Runtime hash matches at deployment, first-exploit previous block 44220864 and campaign end 44222839, and is empty at 40608447; source has no delegatecall, upgrade, selfdestruct or code-selection route. All 4378 top-level victim transactions through the imported exploit anchor include one init and no changePer call. Source-5 init at 40608562:27 selects MATEZ and registers the owner. depositToken() (selector 0xc89039c5) returns zero at 40608561 and MATEZ at 40608562 and 44220864. This initializes intended usage/exposure; the executable truncation defect applies to any valid selected token and already exists at deployment. Oracle pool/token0/token1 are constructor immutables; the oracle correctly prices truncated zero and is not defect-bearing."
    },
    {
      "id": "source-7",
      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-10-04T09:41:06Z",
      "note": "Reviewed full episode loss. Etherscan V2 paginated getLogs from deployment 40608448 through block 44926244: upgrade_package(uint256,uint256) 4382 logs; ClaimCall(uint256,uint256,uint40) 2287 logs; MATEZ Transfer filtered from victim 2287 logs. For each user id with a 2^128 upgrade_package amount, select its ClaimCall only at or after that user first receives the oversized credit. All 110 selected claims are type 3; matching victim Transfer logs in 68 transactions (source-8) sum 8104939811537877595105 base units. Five legitimate claims before the first oversized stake by a later attacker (outside the post-anchor loss population), and ten ordinary later ROI/referral payouts, are excluded. Last fraudulent payout is block 44222742. MATEZ Transfer history 44220865-44259661 has 5209 logs; follow only selected victim payouts through helper/consolidator transfers. Source-9 gives 37 disposals into MATEZ/USDT pool 0xc0319e8f278be2228fd0bad12edfec7b25d16d54; every receipt input equals the tracked stolen MATEZ input, with no added MATEZ. Sold quantity 8092516477619053494203 base units; pool USDT Transfer outflows in those receipts sum 111383939135885293059273 base units, including the two routed USDT->WBNB sales by 0xd4f04374. Both token decimals() are 18 at 44220864. Unsold balance 12423333918824100902 base units is separately valued in source-10. No token depletion is double-counted with proceeds."
